glibc 2.43 turns bsearch into a type-generic macro (__glibc_const_generic,
guarded by __GLIBC_USE (ISOC23), which _GNU_SOURCE enables regardless of
-std=gnu17). That macro breaks the plain prototype h/protoize.h carries for
GCL's own bsearch:

  ../h/../h/protoize.h:106:35: error: expected identifier or '(' before '_Generic'
    106 | /* bsearch.c:5:OF */ extern void *bsearch (const void *key, ...

GCL only ever wants the ordinary function, so drop the macro before the
prototype is parsed. h/include.h is the single place every translation unit
picks protoize.h up from.

--- a/h/include.h
+++ b/h/include.h
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@
 #include "../h/lex.h"
 #include "../h/eval.h"
 
+#undef bsearch
 #include "../h/protoize.h"
 #include "../h/compprotos.h"
 #include "../h/notcomp.h"
